<title>UK: Traf House sale boosts HongkongLand profit.</title>
<headline>Traf House sale boosts HongkongLand profit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million $ unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (cents)		16.89		  vs 6.83</p>
<p> Shr (excluding Traf)   8.64		   vs 7.89</p>
<p> Dividend (cents)	 3.5		    vs 3.5</p>
<p> Net profit		 445.3		  vs 179.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Conglomerate Hong Kong Land Holdings, which released its results in London, said profit after tax -- and excluding a writeback after the $218 million sale of its stake in UK-based Trafalgar House -- rose to $227.7 million from $206.8 million.  </p>
<p> Pretax profit	    478.1		  vs 211.3</p>
<p> Operating profit	 234.7		  vs 220.7</p>
<p> Trafalgar House unit   220.6 profit	 vs 23.1 loss</p>
<p> Tax charge		 32.8		   vs 32.2</p>
<p> Retained profit	  352.9		  vs 87.0</p>
<p> Pay date		   Dec 3</p>
<p> Div registration date  Oct 11</p>
<p> Ex-div date		n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it expected net income in properties -- $247.2 million in the first half -- to show a modest increase in the full year, helped by the $218 exceptional gain from the disposal of Trafalgar House.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
